<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<phyphox version="1.20" locale="en">
  <title>Motion Lab Challenge Demo</title>
  <category>HBCSE-LLNL Labs</category>
  <icon>avx</icon>
  <color>168AAD</color>
  <description>A short demo of motion graphs. You move the phone and stop it. Then you find the moment when its speed is highest, on your own acceleration graph. Phyphox checks the answer.

HOW TO USE
Choose a simple movement. For example, push the phone so that it slides on a table and stops. Or hold the phone flat, stretch your arm out and bring it back. Keep the phone flat and do not tilt or turn it. Move it along one of its sides.
Press Play. The screen counts down 3 s. Keep the phone still during the countdown. When GO appears, make the movement. Then keep the phone still until the screen says Done. The run lasts 5 s. You do not need to press Pause.
Then move the red line to the moment when the speed is highest and press Check. A line of feedback says if the answer is right. After two wrong tries, a hint appears. After a correct answer, the velocity graph appears with the red line on it.
To try again, clear the data with the trash bin and press Play.

WHAT THE MODULE DOES
It uses the data from 0.5 s before GO until the end of the run. It finds the axis with the largest motion by itself and shows it in the graph title. It uses the acceleration without g if the phone has it. The phone is at rest at both ends, so the velocity is zero at both ends. The module subtracts the average acceleration to make this true. Then it calculates the velocity. The graphs show only the moving part, with a short rest on each side. The answer is right if the speed at the red line is at least 85% of the highest speed.
Three numbers near the top of the file set the demo: delay_s (3 s), run_s (5 s) and tol (0.85).

Based on Motion Lab Challenge. Created by Praveen Pathak and David Rakestraw with AI assistance.
Contact: Praveen Pathak, praveen@hbcse.tifr.res.in
All modules and updates: https://github.com/praveen2600/phyphox-modules</description>
  <link label="Email the author">mailto:praveen@hbcse.tifr.res.in</link>
  <link label="All modules on GitHub">https://github.com/praveen2600/phyphox-modules</link>
